I partially but not completely cleaned up the syntax, this is what it looks like:

mean1 <- model$summary.fitted.values[inla.stack.index(stk.full, "prediction")$data,"mean"]
sd1 <- model$summary.fitted.values[inla.stack.index(stk.full, "prediction")$data,"sd"]
m1 <- mean(mean1)
p1 <- 2*pmin(pnorm(m1, mean1, sd1), 1-pnorm(m1, mean1, sd1))

I then select a cutoff of 0.05 as the significance threshold to build a contour.

Would it be similar if I took a brms model output, predicted it to a grid, and then computed the same using the estimate and the est.error columns in the prediction?

